INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-01','mod-shop-orientation','What does the P-A-S-S method stand for when using a fire extinguisher?','["Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep","Point, Activate, Spray, Stop","Prepare, Alert, Signal, Suppress","Pull, Alert, Squeeze, Stand back"]',0,'[0]','Pull the pin, Aim at the base of the fire, Squeeze the handle, Sweep side to side.',1,1,'video','vid-shop-orientation-01-yodLMf',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-02','mod-shop-orientation','Where do you aim a fire extinguisher?','["At the base of the flames","At the top of the flames","At the middle of the fire","Above the fire, letting it fall"]',0,'[0]','Aiming at the flames themselves does nothing. The fuel is at the base.',1,1,'video','vid-shop-orientation-01-yodLMf',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-03','mod-shop-orientation','Which wood dust is the most dangerous to your lungs?','["The fine dust you cannot see hanging in the air","The visible sawdust on the floor","The chips from the planer","The shavings from hand planing"]',0,'[0]','Particles small enough to stay airborne are the ones that reach deep lung tissue. The pile on the floor already fell out of the air and is comparatively harmless.',1,1,'video','vid-shop-orientation-02-TWNyk0',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-04','mod-shop-orientation','A shop looks clean and the air looks clear an hour after cutting. What does that tell you about fine dust?','["Very little - the finest particles stay airborne for hours and are invisible","The air is clear, so the dust has settled and it is safe","Dust only matters while a machine is actually running","Clear air means the dust collector worked perfectly"]',0,'[0]','Fine dust can remain suspended long after the visible cloud is gone, which is why respirators and air filtration matter after the cutting stops.',1,1,'video','vid-shop-orientation-02-TWNyk0',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-05','mod-shop-orientation','Which of these should you remove or secure before running any machine? (Select all that apply.)','["Loose long sleeves","Dangling jewelry and necklaces","Long hair left untied","Gloves at a rotating tool such as a drill press"]',0,'[0,1,2,3]','Anything that can be caught and pulled into a rotating tool. Gloves are the counterintuitive one - they are correct for handling rough stock, wrong at a spinning bit, because a caught glove takes your hand with it.',1,1,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-FVG4a4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-06','mod-shop-orientation','You arrive and find a machine running with nobody at it. What do you do?','["Leave it and find staff - someone may have stepped away mid-operation","Turn it off so it is safe","Use it, since it is already on","Unplug it and move it aside"]',0,'[0]','Shutting down someone else''s running job can ruin their work or their machine. In a shared shop the rule is: if you did not turn it on, do not turn it off - tell staff.',1,0,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-FVG4a4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-07','mod-shop-orientation','Where is the nearest fire extinguisher to the laser cutter at The Box?','["[FILL IN - actual location]","[FILL IN - plausible wrong location]","[FILL IN - plausible wrong location]","[FILL IN - plausible wrong location]"]',0,'[0]','[FILL IN]',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-08','mod-shop-orientation','Someone is injured badly enough to need medical attention. What is the first thing you do?','["[FILL IN - The Box''s actual order of operations; most shops are: call 911 first, then notify staff]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','[FILL IN - and post this on the wall, not only in the quiz]',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-09','mod-shop-orientation','You leave a project in the shop. How long before it becomes property of The Box?','["90 days without written communication with staff","30 days","1 year","It never does"]',0,'[0]','From The Box''s storage and abandoned property policy. Confirm the wording matches the published policy before publishing this question.',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-10','mod-shop-orientation','You have passed this quiz. Which machines may you now use?','["None yet - a knowledge test never grants machine access on its own; you still need a hands-on checkoff with staff","All of them","Only the ones you have watched videos for","Any machine, as long as staff are in the building"]',0,'[0]','This is the single most important thing a member can misunderstand about the learning platform. Worth asking in every module, not just this one.',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-so-11','mod-shop-orientation','Which machines at The Box are allowed to run when nobody is watching them?','["The 3D printers only - anything that cuts with heat or a blade must be attended for every second it runs","Any machine, once you are certified on it","None - every machine must be attended","Any machine, as long as staff are in the building"]',0,'[0]','This is the rule members most reliably get wrong, because they generalise from whichever machine they learned first. A member whose first machine was the Prusa - which is SUPPOSED to run for hours alone - arrives at the plasma table with exactly the wrong instinct. Teach the line, not the individual rules.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-01','mod-table-saw','What is kickback?','["The workpiece being caught by the rising back teeth of the blade and thrown back at the operator","The saw motor stalling under load","The blade slowing down in thick stock","Vibration in the fence during a cut"]',0,'[0]','The back of the blade turns upward and toward you. Anything that lets the workpiece contact it gets launched.',1,1,'video','vid-table-saw-01-Q_8QZF',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-02','mod-table-saw','What does a riving knife do?','["Keeps the kerf open behind the blade so the workpiece cannot pinch or contact the rising teeth","Guides the workpiece against the fence","Reduces splintering on the underside of the cut","Holds the blade guard in position"]',0,'[0]','It is the single most effective anti-kickback device on the saw, which is why it stays on.',1,1,'video','vid-table-saw-01-Q_8QZF',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-03','mod-table-saw','Why must you never use the rip fence and the miter gauge together for a crosscut?','["The offcut becomes trapped between blade and fence and gets thrown","The cut will be out of square","It dulls the blade prematurely","The miter gauge cannot reach the fence"]',0,'[0]','The trapped offcut is the classic kickback setup. Use a stop block clamped ahead of the blade instead.',1,1,'video','vid-table-saw-01-Q_8QZF',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-04','mod-table-saw','Where should you stand while ripping?','["Slightly to one side, out of the line directly behind the blade","Directly behind the blade so the cut stays straight","At the outfeed end of the saw","As far to the left of the table as you can reach"]',0,'[0]','Kickback travels straight back along the blade line. Do not be standing in it.',1,1,'video','vid-table-saw-01-Q_8QZF',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-05','mod-table-saw','You are ripping a narrow strip. When does the push stick become mandatory?','["Once your hand would otherwise pass within a few inches of the blade","Only if the stock is under one inch wide","Only when the guard is removed","Only for stock longer than four feet"]',0,'[0]','The Box should set and post a specific width. Confirm the number before publishing and replace this wording with it.',1,1,'video','vid-table-saw-01-Q_8QZF',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-06','mod-table-saw','A cut binds partway through and the saw starts to bog down. What do you do?','["Hold the workpiece firmly, do not pull it back, turn the saw off and let the blade stop","Pull the workpiece back out of the blade quickly","Push harder to finish the cut","Let go of the workpiece and step back"]',0,'[0]','Pulling back is what feeds the workpiece into the rising teeth. Letting go frees it to be thrown.',1,1,'video','vid-table-saw-01-Q_8QZF',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-07','mod-table-saw','Why should you never cut freehand on a table saw - without the fence or the miter gauge?','["Nothing keeps the workpiece aligned to the blade, so it twists into the blade and kicks back","The cut will not be straight enough for good work","It puts excessive wear on the arbor bearings","It is only unsafe on thin stock"]',0,'[0]','This one is worth stating as an absolute rule rather than a judgment call.',1,1,'video','vid-table-saw-02-fEm1Dj',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-08','mod-table-saw','How high above the workpiece should the blade be set?','["Just above the stock - roughly the height of the gullets between teeth","As high as it goes, for a cleaner cut","Exactly level with the top of the stock","At least two inches above the stock"]',0,'[0]','Lower means less exposed blade and a more downward cutting force. There is a genuine debate about full-height cutting; teach the conservative version in a shared shop.',1,0,'video','vid-table-saw-01-Q_8QZF',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-09','mod-table-saw','Who may change the blade on The Box''s table saw?','["[FILL IN - staff only is the usual answer]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','[FILL IN]',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-ts-10','mod-table-saw','Does The Box''s table saw have a blade-brake safety system (such as SawStop)?','["[FILL IN - the true answer]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','Members behave differently depending on the answer, and a member who assumes a brake exists when it does not is the exact failure this question prevents.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-01','mod-woodshop-basics','How high should the band saw''s upper blade guard be set?','["Just above the workpiece - about a quarter inch","At the top of its travel","Halfway up the column","It does not matter as long as it is above the stock"]',0,'[0]','Lower guard means less exposed blade and better blade support.',1,1,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-Jcn8Gj',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-02','mod-woodshop-basics','What is a relief cut on a band saw?','["A straight cut in to the curve line, so the waste falls away and the blade does not bind in a tight radius","A shallow scoring pass before the full cut","A cut that relieves tension in the blade","A cut made with the fence removed"]',0,'[0]','Tight curves bind the blade; relief cuts are how you avoid forcing it.',1,0,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-Jcn8Gj',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-03','mod-woodshop-basics','After completing a miter saw cut, when may you raise the blade?','["After releasing the trigger and waiting for the blade to stop spinning","Immediately, as soon as the cut is through","As soon as you release the trigger","While still holding the trigger, to clear the kerf"]',0,'[0]','Raising a spinning blade can catch the offcut and throw it, or pull stock up into the blade.',1,1,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-IMJhES',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-04','mod-woodshop-basics','You need a very short piece cut on the miter saw. What is the safe approach?','["Cut it from a longer board using a stop block, so your hands stay well clear","Hold the short piece with your fingers close to the blade","Hold it with pliers","Freehand the cut quickly"]',0,'[0]','Short offcuts near a miter saw blade are one of the most common ways people get hurt on the machine.',1,1,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-IMJhES',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-05','mod-woodshop-basics','Why must you never crosscut - cut across the grain on a short piece - on a jointer?','["The cutterhead can catch the end grain and throw the piece, or pull your hand in","It dulls the knives faster than face jointing","The fence cannot be set square for crosscuts","It leaves a rough surface"]',0,'[0]','A jointer is for edges and faces along the grain, full stop.',1,1,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-V6XzOB',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-06','mod-woodshop-basics','You run a bowed board through the planer and it comes out the same thickness but still bowed. Why?','["A planer references the bottom face and cuts parallel to it - you must flatten one face on the jointer first","The planer knives are dull","You took too heavy a cut","The board was too short for the planer"]',0,'[0]','This is the single most common misunderstanding about the jointer/planer pair and the reason the jointer exists.',1,0,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-V6XzOB',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-07','mod-woodshop-basics','Which stock must never go through the thickness planer?','["Reclaimed or painted wood that may contain nails, screws, staples or grit","Any hardwood over one inch thick","Anything wider than six inches","Freshly jointed stock"]',0,'[0]','Hidden metal destroys the knives and can throw fragments. Check reclaimed stock with a metal detector or do not run it.',1,1,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-88RnZE',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-08','mod-woodshop-basics','On a router table, which way do you feed the workpiece relative to the bit?','["Against the bit''s rotation, so the bit pushes the work back toward you and into the fence","With the bit''s rotation, so the bit pulls the work through","Whichever direction is more comfortable","It only matters for bits over half an inch"]',0,'[0]','Feeding with the rotation is a climb cut - the bit grabs the work and rockets it out of your hands.',1,1,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-QW5Jvk',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-09','mod-woodshop-basics','What is a climb cut?','["Feeding in the same direction as the bit''s rotation, which makes the bit pull the workpiece","Routing uphill on a sloped surface","Taking multiple shallow passes instead of one deep one","Routing with the bit raised above the workpiece"]',0,'[0]','Experienced woodworkers sometimes use light climb cuts deliberately. In a shared shop, teach it as a thing to recognize and avoid.',1,1,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-QW5Jvk',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-wb-10','mod-woodshop-basics','You need to remove a lot of material with a router bit. What is the right approach?','["Several shallow passes, raising the bit between passes","One full-depth pass with a slow feed rate","One full-depth pass with a fast feed rate","Two passes at full depth from opposite directions"]',0,'[0]','Deep single passes are how bits break and workpieces get grabbed.',1,0,'video','vid-woodshop-basics-01-QW5Jvk',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-01','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','Why should you never wear gloves at the drill press?','["A glove caught by the rotating bit pulls your hand in with it","Gloves reduce your grip on the workpiece","Gloves make the depth stop harder to set","Gloves are fine at the drill press"]',0,'[0]','The counterintuitive one. Gloves protect you from splinters and burn you at rotating machinery.',1,1,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-qOT-GK',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-02','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','You are drilling a hole through a small piece of metal or plastic. How should it be held?','["Clamped to the table or held in a drill press vise, never by hand","Firmly by hand, with the other hand on the feed lever","Held with pliers","Held against the column for stability"]',0,'[0]','When the bit breaks through, the workpiece spins. Small, smooth stock spins fastest and cuts worst.',1,1,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-qOT-GK',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-03','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','You are about to use a large-diameter bit. What should happen to the spindle speed?','["It should be reduced - bigger bits run slower","It should be increased - bigger bits need more speed","It makes no difference","It should be set to maximum for a cleaner hole"]',0,'[0]','The rim of a large bit travels much further per revolution. Same rule as any rotating cutter.',1,0,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-qOT-GK',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-04','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','What must you remove from the chuck before switching the drill press on?','["The chuck key","The depth stop","The table insert","The belt cover"]',0,'[0]','A chuck key left in becomes a projectile. Habit: key never leaves your hand.',1,0,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-qOT-GK',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-05','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','Why place a sacrificial backer board under your workpiece?','["It prevents blowout on the underside and protects the drill press table","It raises the work closer to the bit","It keeps the workpiece from spinning","It reduces bit wear"]',0,'[0]','Also stops you from drilling into the table itself, which staff will notice.',1,0,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-qOT-GK',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-06','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','Before using any handheld power tool, which of these should you check? (Select all that apply.)','["The cord and plug for damage","That the guard is present and moves freely","That the workpiece is secured, not held in your lap or hand","That the tool is unplugged before you change a blade or bit"]',0,'[0,1,2,3]','The last one is the one people skip, and it is the one that costs fingers.',1,1,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-FVG4a4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-07','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','You need to change the blade on a circular saw. What is the first step?','["Unplug the tool or remove its battery","Engage the blade lock","Set the depth to zero","Put on gloves"]',0,'[0]','Nothing else matters if the tool can start.',1,1,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-FVG4a4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-08','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','You are cutting a small piece with a jigsaw. Where should your free hand be?','["Well clear of the blade path, with the workpiece clamped to a bench","Holding the workpiece directly beside the cut line","Under the workpiece, supporting it","Steadying the shoe of the saw near the blade"]',0,'[0]','Clamp the work; a hand is not a clamp.',1,1,'video','vid-hand-tools-drill-press-01-FVG4a4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-09','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','Which handheld power tools at The Box may members use without a separate checkoff?','["[FILL IN - The Box''s actual policy]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','[FILL IN. Worth deciding explicitly: ''hand held power tools'' as a category covers everything from a palm sander to a circular saw.]',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-dp-10','mod-hand-tools-drill-press','Where are the drill press bits and the drill press vise kept, and what do you do with them when you finish?','["[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','[FILL IN]',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-01','mod-laser-cutter','Why must PVC never go in the laser?','["It releases chlorine gas, which is toxic to people and corrodes the machine","It melts instead of cutting cleanly","It produces too much smoke for the exhaust","It reflects the beam back at the lens"]',0,'[0]','Both halves matter: it hurts people and it destroys a $20k+ machine from the inside.',1,1,'video','vid-laser-cutter-02-3QBn8U',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-02','mod-laser-cutter','Which of these must NEVER be cut on a CO2 laser? (Select all that apply.)','["PVC / vinyl","Polycarbonate (Lexan)","ABS","Materials containing chlorine of any kind"]',0,'[0,1,2,3]','Polycarbonate burns and yellows rather than cutting; ABS melts and emits cyanide gas. The Box''s posted never-cut list is the authority - update this question to match it exactly.',1,1,'video','vid-laser-cutter-02-3QBn8U',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-03','mod-laser-cutter','The exhaust fan is not running. Can you start a job?','["No - never run the laser without verified exhaust","Yes, for short engraving jobs","Yes, if you open a door","Yes, if the material is only wood"]',0,'[0]','Exhaust is what keeps combustion products out of your lungs and keeps a small flare from becoming a fire.',1,1,'video','vid-laser-cutter-01-uZ6U1l',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-04','mod-laser-cutter','Why may you never leave a running laser unattended, even for a two-minute job?','["A flare-up can start at any moment and become a fire within seconds","The job may finish and waste machine time","The machine may lose focus mid-job","Other members may interrupt the job"]',0,'[0]','The most common way a makerspace loses a laser - and sometimes a building - is someone stepping out to the bathroom.',1,1,'video','vid-laser-cutter-01-uZ6U1l',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-05','mod-laser-cutter','A small flame persists on the material during a cut. What is your first action?','["Stop the job and open the lid only if the flame is out; if it persists, use the extinguisher and get staff","Blow on it","Let the job finish - it usually goes out","Pour water into the bed"]',0,'[0]','Replace this with The Box''s exact posted procedure before publishing. A member should not be improvising here.',1,1,'video','vid-laser-cutter-01-uZ6U1l',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-06','mod-laser-cutter','What is kerf on a laser cutter?','["The width of material the beam removes, which makes cut parts slightly smaller than drawn","The depth the beam penetrates per pass","The distance between the lens and the material","The gap between the honeycomb bed slats"]',0,'[0]','Matters the moment someone tries to make finger joints or press-fit parts.',1,0,'video','vid-laser-cutter-01-OGZZI_',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-07','mod-laser-cutter','Your laser-cut tabs come out slightly too loose in their slots. What is the likely cause?','["Kerf - the beam removed material from both the tab and the slot","The power was set too low","The material was warped","The design was drawn at the wrong scale"]',0,'[0]','Compensating for kerf is the difference between a press fit and a rattle.',1,0,'video','vid-laser-cutter-01-OGZZI_',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-08','mod-laser-cutter','In Inkscape, what distinguishes a line the laser will CUT from one it will ENGRAVE?','["Stroke colour and hairline stroke width, mapped to the laser''s colour settings","The layer it is on","Whether the object is grouped","The document units"]',0,'[0]','Confirm this against The Box''s actual colour mapping in the Epilog driver, then rewrite with your exact convention.',1,0,'video','vid-laser-cutter-01-peDQVh',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-09','mod-laser-cutter','You import a JPEG of a logo and want the laser to cut its outline. What must happen first?','["It must be traced/converted into vector paths - a raster image can only be engraved","It must be converted to greyscale","It must be scaled to 100%","Nothing - the laser cuts raster images directly"]',0,'[0]','The raster/vector distinction is the number one thing that sends a member back to the computer.',1,0,'video','vid-laser-cutter-01-peDQVh',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-lc-10','mod-laser-cutter','You brought your own sheet material from home. What must you do before cutting it?','["[FILL IN - The Box''s material approval process; most spaces require staff sign-off and an SDS or known material type]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','This is how PVC gets into a laser. Make the process explicit and make this question mandatory.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-01','mod-3d-printing','What does a good first layer look like?','["Lines squished slightly flat, touching each other with no gaps, evenly stuck to the bed","Round lines with visible gaps between them","Lines barely touching the bed, easy to peel","A translucent, very thin sheet"]',0,'[0]','Most failures on a shared printer are visible in the first two minutes. Teaching members to look is worth more than any other lesson here.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-02-Z0VLR6',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-02','mod-3d-printing','The first layer is not sticking and the print is turning into a bird''s nest. What should you do?','["Cancel the print immediately and tell staff","Let it run and see if it recovers","Push the filament down with your fingers","Increase the print speed"]',0,'[0]','A nine-hour spaghetti print wastes filament, machine time and someone else''s slot, and can damage the printer.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-02-Z0VLR6',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-03','mod-3d-printing','Why must the print bed be free of fingerprints and grease?','["Oils prevent adhesion and cause the print to lift","Oils burn and produce fumes","Oils damage the PEI sheet permanently","It only matters for large prints"]',0,'[0]','Clean the sheet with IPA, and handle it by the edges.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-02-Z0VLR6',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-04','mod-3d-printing','You need a part that will sit in a car in summer. Which filament is the wrong choice?','["PLA - it softens at temperatures a parked car easily reaches","PETG","ABS","ASA"]',0,'[0]','The classic beginner surprise: a perfectly good PLA phone mount deforms on the dashboard.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-01-Or1FP4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-05','mod-3d-printing','Which filament is the easiest to print and the default for most makerspace work?','["PLA","ABS","Nylon","Polycarbonate"]',0,'[0]','Low temperature, minimal warping, no enclosure needed, least fumes.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-01-Or1FP4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-06','mod-3d-printing','What does the slicer actually do?','["Converts a 3D model into layer-by-layer toolpath instructions (G-code) the printer can run","Shrinks the model to fit the bed","Repairs errors in the 3D model","Compresses the file for the printer''s SD card"]',0,'[0]','Members who understand this stop treating the slicer as a mystery box.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-01-_kIqMP',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-07','mod-3d-printing','Where do you find out how long a print will take before you start it?','["The slicer''s estimate after slicing","The printer''s display once the print begins","By measuring the file size","There is no way to know in advance"]',0,'[0]','Tie this directly to billing: The Box''s machine rate model charges per print-hour from the slicer estimate, so members need to know where that number lives.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-01-_kIqMP',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-08','mod-3d-printing','Your model has a steep overhang. What does the slicer need in order to print it?','["Support material, or a different part orientation","A higher infill percentage","A slower first layer","A larger brim"]',0,'[0]','Rotating the part is usually the better answer, and supports are the fallback.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-01-_kIqMP',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-09','mod-3d-printing','In Tinkercad, how do you make a hole in a solid shape?','["Place a shape set to ''Hole'', position it, then group it with the solid","Use the eraser tool","Set the solid''s opacity to zero","Subtract it in the export settings"]',0,'[0]','Solid/hole plus group is the entire mental model of Tinkercad. A member who has this can build most things.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-01-SXVK-I',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-3d-10','mod-3d-printing','What file format do you export from Tinkercad to bring into the slicer?','["STL (or 3MF)","SVG","DXF","G-code"]',0,'[0]','The Tinkercad → STL → slicer → G-code chain is the whole pipeline; worth a diagram in the lesson text.',1,0,'video','vid-3d-printing-01-SXVK-I',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-01','mod-resin-printing','Which gloves must you wear when handling uncured resin?','["Nitrile","Latex","Cotton work gloves","Any glove, as long as it is intact"]',0,'[0]','Latex is permeable to the chemicals in photopolymer resin and offers little protection. Nitrile only.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-02','mod-resin-printing','Uncured resin gets on your bare skin. What do you do?','["Wash it off immediately with soap and water, and never with IPA on skin","Let it dry, then peel it off","Wipe it with an IPA-soaked paper towel","Nothing - cured resin is inert"]',0,'[0]','IPA on skin drives the resin further in and strips the skin''s barrier. Soap and water, immediately.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-03','mod-resin-printing','Why does repeated skin contact with uncured resin matter even when it does not hurt at the time?','["Photopolymer resin is a sensitizer - repeated exposure can produce a permanent allergy","It stains the skin","It causes immediate chemical burns","It does not matter if you wash promptly"]',0,'[0]','This is the single most important fact in the module. People develop resin allergies after months of casual handling, and then they can never work with it again.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-04','mod-resin-printing','What is the hazard with the IPA used for washing prints?','["It is flammable and its vapour is an inhalation hazard","It is corrosive to skin","It reacts with cured resin","There is no significant hazard"]',0,'[0]','Keep it capped, keep it away from ignition sources, and keep the area ventilated. A plasma table is in the same building - worth knowing where the IPA lives relative to it.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-05','mod-resin-printing','What must happen to failed prints, supports and drips before they go in the trash?','["They must be fully cured under UV first","Nothing - they can be binned as-is","They must be rinsed in IPA","They must be double-bagged"]',0,'[0]','Uncured resin in a bin is a hazardous-waste problem and a contact hazard for whoever empties it.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-06','mod-resin-printing','Which of these are required before you start a resin print? (Select all that apply.)','["Nitrile gloves on","Eye protection on","Ventilation running","Knowing where the liquid resin waste container is"]',0,'[0,1,2,3]','All four. If any one is not true, do not start.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-07','mod-resin-printing','What does the wash station actually do?','["Removes uncured resin from the surface of the print using IPA","Cures the print","Removes support structures","Dries the print"]',0,'[0]','Wash then cure, in that order. Curing a print with uncured resin still on it locks a sticky layer onto the surface.',1,0,'video','vid-resin-printing-01-QJogbB',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-08','mod-resin-printing','Why must a print be washed before it is cured, and not the other way round?','["Curing traps the uncured surface resin, leaving a permanently tacky, contaminated part","Curing first makes supports harder to remove","Washing after curing damages the print","The order does not matter"]',0,'[0]','Also means a ''finished'' part that still carries uncured resin - a contact hazard for whoever handles it next.',1,0,'video','vid-resin-printing-01-QJogbB',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-09','mod-resin-printing','A print has failed and part of it is stuck to the film at the bottom of the vat. What do you do?','["Stop and get staff - digging at the FEP film with a tool can puncture it and dump resin into the machine","Scrape it off with the metal spatula","Run another print; it will clear itself","Peel it off with your fingers"]',0,'[0]','A punctured FEP means resin in the printer''s optics and a repair bill. This is the most common way a shared resin printer gets damaged.',1,1,'video','vid-resin-printing-02-aIADEF',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-10','mod-resin-printing','Where does used IPA go when it is too dirty to wash with?','["Sealed labeled used-IPA container for staff to take to King County Moderate Risk Waste — never down the drain","Pour it down the sink with plenty of water","Leave it open next to the wash station to evaporate","Dump it in the regular trash once it looks clear"]',0,'[0]','Best-practice placeholder for The Box. Liquid IPA is household hazardous waste in King County; do not drain it. Staff handle the drop-off. Edit if shop policy differs.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-rs-11','mod-resin-printing','Your resin print will take six hours. May you leave it running and go home?','["Yes - printers are the exception; they may run unattended","No - no machine at The Box may run unattended","Only if staff are in the building","Only if another member agrees to watch it"]',0,'[0]','Printers may run unattended. The laser and the plasma table may not, even when you are certified and working alone. Learn the line: machines that cut with heat or a blade get watched every second; printers do not. Confirm what The Box requires before walking away - lid closed, ventilation running, name and finish time on the machine.',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-01','mod-vinyl-cutter','What does ''weeding'' mean in vinyl work?','["Removing the excess vinyl from around the design after cutting","Cleaning the cutting mat","Trimming the vinyl sheet to size before loading","Removing air bubbles after application"]',0,'[0]','The step that takes the longest and that nobody warns beginners about.',1,0,'video','vid-vinyl-cutter-01-GHJWxE',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-02','mod-vinyl-cutter','What is a ''kiss cut''?','["Cutting through the vinyl but not through its paper backing","Cutting the design twice for a cleaner edge","Cutting two designs at once","Cutting through both vinyl and backing"]',0,'[0]','Cut settings that go all the way through ruin the design and score the mat or the machine''s strip.',1,0,'video','vid-vinyl-cutter-01-GHJWxE',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-03','mod-vinyl-cutter','What should you always do before running a full cut on unfamiliar material?','["Run a test cut and check the depth","Double the blade depth for safety","Cut at the slowest speed available","Cut a mirrored version first"]',0,'[0]','Ten seconds of test cut versus a ruined sheet.',1,0,'video','vid-vinyl-cutter-01-GHJWxE',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-04','mod-vinyl-cutter','You are cutting heat transfer vinyl (HTV) for a shirt. What must you remember in the software?','["Mirror the design before cutting, and load the vinyl shiny-carrier-side down","Increase the blade depth to maximum","Cut it at the same settings as adhesive vinyl","Weed before cutting"]',0,'[0]','Forgetting to mirror is the single most common HTV mistake and it is unrecoverable.',1,0,'video','vid-vinyl-cutter-01-GHJWxE',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-05','mod-vinyl-cutter','What is transfer tape used for?','["Lifting the weeded design off its backing and placing it on the final surface in one piece","Holding the vinyl to the cutting mat","Protecting the design after application","Masking areas that should not be cut"]',0,'[0]','Without it, a multi-piece design has to be placed letter by letter.',1,0,'video','vid-vinyl-cutter-01-mJ28gA',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-06','mod-vinyl-cutter','When does the vinyl need to be on a cutting mat?','["When the material has no backing rigid enough to feed on its own, or when cutting sheets rather than roll stock","Always, for every material","Never on the Cameo 4","Only for paper"]',0,'[0]','Confirm against The Box''s actual materials and update - the Cameo 4 handles some roll media matless.',1,0,'video','vid-vinyl-cutter-01-mJ28gA',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-07','mod-vinyl-cutter','Your cut is tearing the vinyl and cutting into the backing. What is the most likely fix?','["Reduce blade depth and/or force","Increase the speed","Use a new mat","Switch to a thicker vinyl"]',0,'[0]','Too much blade is the usual culprit, and it damages the machine''s cutting strip over time.',1,0,'video','vid-vinyl-cutter-01-mJ28gA',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-08','mod-vinyl-cutter','What does ''Print and Cut'' with registration marks let you do?','["Print a design on an inkjet printer and have the Cameo cut precisely around it","Cut two copies simultaneously","Print the cut settings to a file","Cut and score in a single pass"]',0,'[0]','Ties the vinyl cutter to The Box''s laminators and custom print products.',1,0,'video','vid-vinyl-cutter-01-mJ28gA',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-09','mod-vinyl-cutter','Does The Box supply vinyl, or do members bring their own? What does it cost?','["[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','[FILL IN - the membership pitch lists the vinyl cutter as included with no hourly charge, but consumables are a separate question.]',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-vc-10','mod-vinyl-cutter','What do you do with the cutting mat and blade when you finish?','["[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','[FILL IN. Mats are consumable and get ruined by being left sticky-side up or with vinyl scraps on them.]',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-01','mod-sewing','What is the bobbin?','["The lower spool that supplies the underside thread of a stitch","The spool holder on top of the machine","The wheel that advances the fabric","The dial that sets stitch length"]',0,'[0]','A stitch is two threads: needle thread from above, bobbin thread from below.',1,0,'video','vid-sewing-machine-01-BtX2zc',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-02','mod-sewing','Where must the presser foot be when you thread the machine?','["Raised - this releases the tension discs so the thread seats properly","Lowered, to hold the thread in place","Removed entirely","It makes no difference"]',0,'[0]','The most common cause of a machine that ''won''t sew right'' after threading, and almost nobody explains why.',1,0,'video','vid-sewing-machine-01-fzlT-S',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-03','mod-sewing','Your stitches are looping and messy on the underside of the fabric. What is the most likely cause?','["The upper thread is not seated in the tension discs - rethread with the presser foot up","The bobbin is wound too tightly","The needle is too small","The fabric is too thick"]',0,'[0]','Almost always an upper-threading problem, even though the symptom appears underneath.',1,0,'video','vid-sewing-machine-01-fzlT-S',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-04','mod-sewing','How should you guide fabric through the machine?','["Let the feed dogs pull it, guiding lightly - never pull or push the fabric","Pull it firmly from behind to keep it straight","Push it steadily from the front","Hold it still and let the needle walk"]',0,'[0]','Pulling bends and snaps needles, which then fly. The one genuinely safety-relevant habit at a sewing machine.',1,1,'video','vid-sewing-machine-01-BtX2zc',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-05','mod-sewing','What is backstitching and when do you use it?','["Sewing a few stitches in reverse at the start and end of a seam to lock it","Sewing the seam a second time for strength","Sewing from the back side of the fabric","A decorative stitch pattern"]',0,'[0]','Without it, seams pull out.',1,0,'video','vid-sewing-machine-01-BtX2zc',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-06','mod-sewing','Which way should the handwheel be turned when you turn it by hand?','["Toward you","Away from you","Either direction","Only while the machine is running"]',0,'[0]','Turning it backwards can unthread the machine or jam the timing.',1,0,'video','vid-sewing-machine-01-BtX2zc',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-07','mod-sewing','You are about to sew heavy denim after finishing a project in quilting cotton. What should change?','["The needle - heavier fabric needs a heavier needle","Nothing","The bobbin thread colour only","The machine''s power setting"]',0,'[0]','Wrong needle for the fabric is the second most common cause of skipped stitches and broken needles.',1,0,'video','vid-sewing-machine-01-BtX2zc',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-08','mod-sewing','Before you start sewing, where should both thread tails be?','["Pulled to the back, under the presser foot","Left loose at the front","Wrapped around the handwheel","Cut flush at the needle"]',0,'[0]','Loose tails at the front get pulled down into the bobbin case and cause a nest.',1,0,'video','vid-sewing-machine-01-fzlT-S',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-09','mod-sewing','The needle breaks while you are sewing. What do you do?','["[FILL IN - The Box''s procedure. Most spaces: stop, find every fragment, tell staff, do not replace the needle yourself unless trained]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','[FILL IN]',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-sw-10','mod-sewing','Does The Box supply thread, needles and bobbins, or do members bring their own?','["[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]","[FILL IN]"]',0,'[0]','[FILL IN - relevant to the bowl cozy and stocking classes too.]',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,1,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-01','mod-cnc-plasma','Plasma cutting produces which hazards? (Select all that apply.)','["Metal fume that must be ventilated or extracted","Intense UV and IR radiation that burns eyes and skin","Sparks and molten metal spatter","High voltage at the torch"]',0,'[0,1,2,3]','This machine is categorically more dangerous than anything else at The Box and the cert should reflect that.',1,1,'video','vid-cnc-plasma-01-Okyko4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-02','mod-cnc-plasma','What is ''arc eye'' (photokeratitis)?','["A painful burn of the cornea from UV exposure, often not felt until hours later","Eye strain from watching the torch","Temporary blindness from the flash","Irritation from metal fume"]',0,'[0]','The delay is what makes it dangerous - people think they got away with it and do it again.',1,1,'video','vid-cnc-plasma-01-Okyko4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-03','mod-cnc-plasma','Who needs eye protection when the plasma table is cutting?','["Everyone in line of sight, not only the operator","Only the operator","Only people within six feet","Nobody, if the table has a water bed"]',0,'[0]','This drives a shop-layout decision, not just a PPE decision: where can bystanders stand while the table runs?',1,1,'video','vid-cnc-plasma-01-Okyko4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-04','mod-cnc-plasma','Which materials must never be cut on a plasma table?','["Galvanized or zinc-coated metal without dedicated extraction, and anything coated or painted with unknown finishes","Mild steel over 1/4 inch","Aluminium of any kind","Stainless steel"]',0,'[0]','Zinc fume causes metal fume fever. Confirm The Box''s own material list and rewrite this to match it.',1,1,'video','vid-cnc-plasma-01-Okyko4',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-05','mod-cnc-plasma','Before starting a cut, what must be verified about the workpiece?','["It is clamped or held flat and the ground clamp has solid contact with it","It is centred on the table","It is at room temperature","It is free of mill scale"]',0,'[0]','A lifting workpiece collides with the torch; a bad ground makes the arc unreliable and unsafe.',1,1,'video','vid-cnc-plasma-01-Y0YDV1',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-06','mod-cnc-plasma','Where must your hands never be during a cut?','["Anywhere on the table or in the machine''s travel envelope","Only directly under the torch","Only on the gantry rails","Hands may rest on the table edge"]',0,'[0]','A CNC gantry does not know your hand is there and will not stop.',1,1,'video','vid-cnc-plasma-01-Y0YDV1',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-07','mod-cnc-plasma','What is the correct order of the plasma workflow?','["Design → toolpath in VCarve → post to G-code → load in Mach4 → set origin → cut","Design → load in Mach4 → cut → toolpath","Toolpath → design → cut","Design → cut → post-process"]',0,'[0]','Members who understand the chain stop asking staff why the file ''won''t open in Mach4''.',1,1,'video','vid-cnc-plasma-02-STBwZN',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-08','mod-cnc-plasma','Where is the emergency stop, and when do you use it?','["Within reach before you start any job - use it for any unexpected motion, collision or fire","Only for a machine fault","Only if someone is injured","It should not be used; use the software stop instead"]',0,'[0]','Replace with the E-stop''s actual location at The Box. Every member should touch it once during the checkoff so their hand knows where it is - especially since they will be cutting alone.',1,1,'video','vid-cnc-plasma-02-STBwZN',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-09','mod-cnc-plasma','In VCarve, what is a toolpath?','["The instructions describing how the machine moves and cuts to produce your design","The physical path the material takes through the machine","The folder where files are saved","The route the design takes from computer to machine"]',0,'[0]','The design is not the job. The toolpath is the job.',1,0,'video','vid-cnc-plasma-01-xKTpAo',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-pl-10','mod-cnc-plasma','You are certified on the plasma table and you are the only person in the shop. Which is true?','["You may cut, but you must stay with the machine for the whole cut","You may not cut without staff present","You may cut and step away once the job is running","You may cut only if another certified member is present"]',0,'[0]','Confirmed policy at The Box: solo operation is allowed, unattended operation is not. Because nobody else is in the room, everything else in this module is not advisory - it is the whole safety system.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-01','mod-embroidery-machine','While the embroidery machine is stitching, what should you do with the fabric?','["Let the hoop move the fabric — do not pull or push it","Pull gently ahead of the needle to keep tension","Hold the fabric taut with both hands beside the hoop","Push from behind to speed dense designs"]',0,'[0]','Pulling while stitching bends and breaks needles.',1,1,'video','vid-embroidery-machine-01--gY539',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-02','mod-embroidery-machine','A needle breaks mid-design. What is the first priority?','["Stop, find every fragment, and tell staff before replacing the needle","Install a new needle immediately and resume","Raise the speed and finish the design","Cut the design out of the hoop and start over"]',0,'[0]','Loose needle fragments damage the machine and cut fingers. Shop policy: staff before restart if unsure.',1,1,'video','vid-embroidery-machine-01--gY539',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-03','mod-embroidery-machine','Where does a pre-wound bobbin typically go on a Brother embroidery machine?','["In the bobbin case under the needle plate, oriented per the machine''s diagram","On the top spool pin next to the upper thread","Inside the hoop under the fabric","It is optional for embroidery"]',0,'[0]','Bobbin orientation is model-specific — follow the diagram on the machine.',1,0,'video','vid-embroidery-machine-01--gY539',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-04','mod-embroidery-machine','How do members usually load custom designs onto a Brother PE-class machine?','["USB drive with a supported embroidery file format","Email the design to the machine","Print the design on paper and scan it","Only built-in designs are allowed"]',0,'[0]','Confirm The Box''s accepted formats (often PES) at the station.',1,0,'video','vid-embroidery-machine-01--gY539',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-05','mod-embroidery-machine','Which stabilizer should you reach for first on a stretchy t-shirt?','["Cutaway","Tearaway only","No stabilizer","Water-soluble only, with nothing behind the fabric"]',0,'[0]','Cutaway stays with the garment and supports stretch fabrics through washing.',1,0,'video','vid-embroidery-machine-01-472kqi',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-06','mod-embroidery-machine','Tearaway stabilizer is generally best for:','["Stable woven fabrics where you want to remove the backing after stitching","Every knit garment","Replacing the bobbin thread","Lubricating the needle"]',0,'[0]','Tearaway on stretch knits is a common cause of puckering.',1,0,'video','vid-embroidery-machine-01-472kqi',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-07','mod-embroidery-machine','When hooping, how tight should the fabric be?','["Taut like a drum without stretching the grain of the fabric","Loose so the hoop does not leave marks","Stretched hard in every direction after the screw is tight","Only the stabilizer needs to be tight"]',0,'[0]','Over-stretching in the hoop causes puckering when you unhoop.',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-08','mod-embroidery-machine','Why must excess fabric be kept clear of the embroidery arm?','["Loose fabric can be caught and sewn into the arm or design","It blocks the touchscreen","It cools the motor","It does not matter"]',0,'[0]','Caught fabric ruins the project and can damage the machine.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-09','mod-embroidery-machine','Does The Box supply stabilizer, bobbins, and embroidery thread?','["Best practice: shop stocks basics for checkoff and classes; members bring specialty thread — confirm posted consumable policy","Everything is free unlimited","Members must bring a whole machine","Only needles are supplied"]',0,'[0]','Provisional answer — edit when consumable policy is posted.',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-em-10','mod-embroidery-machine','You passed this quiz. May you embroider unsupervised tomorrow?','["Not yet — you still need a staff hands-on checkoff for machine access","Yes, the quiz unlocks the badge","Yes, if another member watches","Yes, after one practice at home"]',0,'[0]','Knowledge pass is not machine access.',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-01','mod-sublimation','Before printing a design for a shirt, what must usually happen to the artwork?','["It must be mirrored so it reads correctly after pressing","It must be converted to greyscale","It must be printed twice","Nothing — mirror only applies to vinyl"]',0,'[0]','Forgetting to mirror is the classic first failure.',1,0,'video','vid-sublimation-01-tJGG1l',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-02','mod-sublimation','Which garment takes sublimation dye best?','["Light-coloured high-polyester (ideally 100% polyester) fabric","100% cotton dark hoodie","Wool coat","Any fabric if you press longer"]',0,'[0]','Dye bonds to polyester; cotton and dark garments are the wrong blank.',1,0,'video','vid-sublimation-01-tJGG1l',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-03','mod-sublimation','Why stay with the heat press while it is closed on a job?','["The platen is hot enough to burn, and a press left alone is a fire and injury risk","The printer needs the network from the press","Sublimation only works if you watch it","You do not — heat presses may run overnight"]',0,'[0]','Treat the press like other heat equipment: attended for the cycle.',1,1,'video','vid-sublimation-01-Nu5P-Y',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-04','mod-sublimation','What usually causes ghosting (a blurry double image)?','["The transfer shifted when the press opened or closed","The printer was offline","The shirt was 100% polyester","The design was mirrored"]',0,'[0]','Tape the transfer; do not bump the paper while hot.',1,1,'video','vid-sublimation-02-7NxQRs',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-05','mod-sublimation','Faded or dull colours after pressing most often mean:','["Time, temperature, pressure, or substrate was wrong for a full dye transfer","The design used too much white","The press was attended","The paper was mirrored correctly"]',0,'[0]','Use The Box''s posted chart, not a random YouTube temperature.',1,0,'video','vid-sublimation-02-7NxQRs',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-06','mod-sublimation','What is Sawgrass Print Manager (or Print Utility) for?','["Applying the right colour profile, quality, and often mirroring for sublimation output","Controlling the heat press temperature only","Digitizing embroidery designs","Billing machine time"]',0,'[0]','Print through the shop utility, not a generic driver guess.',1,0,'video','vid-sublimation-01-m4k5xJ',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-07','mod-sublimation','Why put butcher paper inside a shirt and over the transfer?','["To stop ink blow-through from staining the back of the shirt or the press platen","To cool the platen faster","To make cotton accept dye","It is only decorative"]',0,'[0]','Protect the press and the garment.',1,0,'video','vid-sublimation-01-Nu5P-Y',1,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-08','mod-sublimation','Before closing the heat press, which are required? (Select all that apply.)','["Transfer secured so it cannot shift","Protective paper / covering on the platen side","Knowing the posted time and temperature for that blank","Leaving the area once the timer starts"]',0,'[0,1,2]','The last option is wrong — stay with the press.',1,1,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-09','mod-sublimation','Who may change the heat press temperature setpoints on The Box''s press?','["Best practice: use the posted chart; only staff change machine defaults — members select the listed setting for their blank","Anyone may reprogram defaults for the day","Only the previous user","Temperature does not matter for sublimation"]',0,'[0]','Provisional — edit to match posted shop policy.',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO Question VALUES('q-su-10','mod-sublimation','You passed this quiz. Which machines may you use?','["None yet — knowledge pass still requires a hands-on checkoff","Printer and press immediately","Only the printer","Any textile machine in the building"]',0,'[0]','Same rule as every other machine module.',1,0,'shop-policy',NULL,0,0,1788721200000,1788721200000,NULL);
